        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Wade Watts, Thurgood Marshall, Martin Luther King, Miller Newman, J. C. Watts\n- Organizations: NAACP, Oklahoma Sooners, Canadian Football League\n- Places: Oklahoma\n- Events: American civil rights movement\n- Roles: mentor, politician, college football quarterback, former congressman\n\nFacts:\n- During the American civil rights movement, Wade Watts worked with Thurgood Marshall and developed a friendship with Martin Luther King.\n- Wade Watts has been cited as a mentor by Miller Newman, the current leader of the NAACP in Oklahoma.\n- Wade Watts has also been cited as a mentor by his nephew, former congressman J. C. Watts.\n- J. C. Watts, whose full name is Julius Caesar \"J. C.\" Watts Jr., was born on November 18, 1957.\n- J. C. Watts is an American politician from Oklahoma.\n- J. C. Watts was a college football quarterback for the Oklahoma Sooners and later played professionally in the Canadian Football League.",
